WINapk
======

WINapk is a from-scratch re-implementation inspired by and forked from the
architecture of ApkStart (https://github.com/RoutineMiku/apkstart),
Copyright (c) RoutineMiku, distributed under the MIT License.

Binary-XML (AXML) and resource-table (ARSC) parsing logic in
crates/winapk-install was ported to Rust from apkstart's
src/core/axml.js and src/core/arsc.js (MIT License).

The upstream project's UX model — "one Android app = one clean Windows
window, double-click .apk to install" — is preserved; the engine,
orchestrator, display host and host/guest channels are new code.
